// Where the art is: named regions of the sprite sheet. Facts about the art only; which art a
// biome or object kind uses, and how it is placed, is chosen in tiles.ron and objects.ron.
//
// Rects are (x, y, width, height) in sheet pixels, y down.
//
// tiles:   ground tile regions; all must have the same size. tiles.ron `regions` maps
//          texture names onto them. Each surface has a height ladder, numbered from the
//          highest (`_0`, the leftmost tile of its sheet row).
// sprites: object art per surface; each entry is a list of variants, one picked per object.
//   pivot: the art's foot point in pixels inside its rect (default: bottom center,
//          (width / 2, height)). It sits on the object's footprint, and draw order follows it.
// sheets:  further sheets, each `(image, sprites)` like the main one; see the end of the file.
//
// The item icons in the sheet's bottom row are not world art and are not listed.
(
    image: "textures/atlas.png",
    tiles: {
        "regolith_0": (32, 32, 32, 32),
        "regolith_1": (64, 32, 32, 32),
        "regolith_2": (96, 32, 32, 32),
